=begin pod

=TITLE Writing to Learn

William K. Zissner has written a book called "Writing to Learn".  The basic 
premise is that, by writing about something, you can organise your thoughts more 
clearly, and that, by so doing, you learn yourself.  

One way of learning about Raku is to write about it.  

You can use the L<resources|https://raku.org/resources/> to learn Raku, and 
L<write|https://planet.raku.org/> about your experience along the way! Let us 
know when you do write something if you want to share it with the larger Raku 
community (you should!).  The best way to do so is to join #raku on IRC, and say 
C<weekly: URL>, where C<URL> is the URL of the article you've written.  

Some writing topics could be programs you've written, tricks you've learned, 
cool things about the Raku, etc. Because of your fresh perspective as a learner, 
writing educational/training material would be a great idea as well.

If anything is Less Than Awesome in your experience you can 
L<chat with us|https://raku.org/community/irc>, or open an issue on the 
L<User Experience|https://github.com/perl6/user-experience>  repository.

=end pod
